\pard\sa140 \fs21 \b Re: Application for Digital Transformation Specialist, Ref. JR4434 (Grade 4, three-year project contract)\b0 \par
\pard\sa140 \fs21 Dear Members of the Selection Panel,\par
\pard\sa140 \fs21 I am applying for the Digital Transformation Specialist post (JR4434) within the Operations Management Team's Change & Engagement function. For more than thirteen years I have done, day to day, much of what this role describes: turning complex subject-matter knowledge into clear, accurate, accessible guidance; keeping documentation and knowledge repositories current and well organised; coordinating subject matter experts, technical teams and end users through platform and process change; and \'97 most importantly \'97 helping colleagues actually adopt new systems and new ways of working.\par
\pard\sa140 \fs21 At Palika Live I coordinated the move from [old system] to [new platform] for [N] users: mapping the workflow, identifying impacts and risks, writing the user guides and SOPs, recording short how-to videos, and planning the communications and training delivered ahead of go-live. Adoption reached [X]% within [N] weeks, and the remaining support queries were analysed and fed back into the guidance. That is close to the ERP transformation work in the vacancy \'97 supporting the Change Manager with impact assessments, stakeholder mapping and business readiness, and acting as the coordination point between SMEs, change managers and end users. I have also authored and maintained editorial style guides, SOPs and onboarding material under a scheduled review cycle, and rebuilt our central content repository \'97 taxonomy, naming conventions, permissions and version control \'97 so colleagues find one current version rather than several competing ones. Maintaining Workday Help content and a central repository of user documentation is therefore work I have done at scale, and I know how quickly documentation loses trust when it falls out of date.\par
\pard\sa140 \fs21 My background is journalism, so writing for different audiences \'97 a first-time end user or a senior stakeholder \'97 is my core craft, as are managing several concurrent projects against fixed deadlines and keeping everyone informed. Thirteen years of research, verification and quality control have also given me a strongly analytical habit: gather the evidence, check it, find where the process fails, and make a data-driven recommendation.\par
\pard\sa140 \fs21 On Workday HCM specifically, I am transparent: my hands-on experience to date is with content management systems and enterprise collaboration platforms rather than Workday, and my exposure to HR and finance processes comes from daily use of rostering, point-of-sale and stock systems \'97 and from onboarding new starters onto them in earlier operational roles. What I can offer is a proven ability to learn an enterprise system quickly, become the person colleagues ask for help, and then document and teach it to others. [Workday self-study sentence: I have begun familiarising myself with Workday HCM's structure and with how Workday Help content is organised through (course name). \'97 If you have not started, replace with: I have scheduled Workday HCM fundamentals training for my first weeks in post.] I would welcome the chance to build hands-on proficiency within your team.\par
\pard\sa140 \fs21 The chance to support digital transformation at an institute whose open biological data and tools underpin research worldwide is exactly the public-purpose work I want the next stage of my career to serve. My degree in Mass Communication & Journalism, with thirteen years of international-facing editorial and digital work, fits the related-discipline profile for this post, and I am fully prepared to relocate to Hinxton for the three-year project.\par
\pard\sa140 \fs21 Thank you for considering my application. My CV is enclosed; writing samples, documentation examples and references are available on request. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my change, content and coordination experience can support the Operations Management Team and EMBL-EBI's ERP transformation.\par
\pard\sa140 \fs21 Yours sincerely,\par
\pard\sa140 \fs21 Liladhar Koirala\par
\pard\sa140 \fs21 Enclosure: Curriculum Vitae (Ref. JR4434)\par}